# Browser
# Craft in the client (CR 702.167a). Dire Flail's menu offers its craft ability with its cost, "Craft with artifact
# {3}{R}{R}" (Equip is not, with no creature to equip). Activated, the choice of materials is asked as craft's own: the
# artifacts Bot1 controls (two Moxen, a Sol Ring) and the Black Lotus card in its graveyard are offered together, and the
# caption says where they may come from and that they are exiled. The Lotus is chosen from the graveyard and confirmed
# with "Exile it"; the Flail returns as Dire Blunderbuss. The mana is paid exactly (the Lotus's leftover red, the Mountain, one
# Mox and the Ring): mana left over in the pool would ask which to spend first, and the title is read at that question.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mountain
Black Lotus
Dire Flail
Mox Ruby
Mox Ruby
Sol Ring
Island
Island x10

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mountain.Play
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Red)
Bot1.Hand.Dire Flail.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Sol Ring.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Dire Flail.Activate(Ability: Craft)
? Client.Bot1.Menu = Craft with artifact {3}{R}{R}
Bot1.Battlefield.Mountain.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby#1.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Sol Ring.Activate
? Client.Bot1.Prompt.Title = Dire Flail: craft - choose an artifact you control or an artifact card from your graveyard to exile
Bot1.Choose(craft materials)
Bot1.Choose(Graveyard.Black Lotus)
? Client.Bot1.Confirm = Exile it
[T1 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield = Mountain; Mox Ruby; Mox Ruby; Sol Ring; Dire Blunderbuss
Exile = Black Lotus
